  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 514.07 Time for Display",
  "priorExpiration": "2012-03-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 514.07 Time for Display. The owner of a properly registered vehicle for the succeeding year may display the registration plates or decals for that year in place of those plates or decals of the current year. In such an event the registrant shall carry both the current and succeeding certificates of registration in the vehicle.\n\nSource. #7972, eff 10-17-03 (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Saf-C 500); ss by #9995, INTERIM, eff 9-17-11, EXPIRED: 3-15-12\n\nNew. #10135, eff 5-23-12; ss by #13521, eff 1-13-23 (formerly Saf-C 515.07)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c500.html"
